(1019, 808, '59', 'CLEOVIN C. SILONG', 'The laptop has already been reformatted, and MS Office has been Installed', '2026-01-21', '05:07 PM'),
(1020, 811, '58', 'MARIETTA L. CHUA', 'Vin for your appropriate action', '2026-01-27', '10:42 AM'),
(1021, 810, '58', 'MARIETTA L. CHUA', 'Vin for your appropriate action', '2026-01-27', '10:29 AM'),
(1022, 809, '1915', 'Emmanuel D. Gonzales', 'Upon Checking:The printer indicator light continuously blinking, indicating a system error and need to reset.Action Taken:Performed printer reset procedure.Continue monitoring the printer after the reset and perform nozzle check and head cleaning as needed to ensure proper print quality and functionality.', '2026-01-22', '11:40 AM'),
(1023, 784, '1915', 'Emmanuel D. Gonzales', 'Upon Checking:The printer was found to have hardened tissue paper and a staple wire stuck inside the paper feed mechanism, causing blockage and triggering the blinking indicator light.Action Taken: Carefully removed the hardened tissue from the printer and other hard object . However, due to the blockage, the panel flex cable and printer head were damaged. Status DEFFECTIVE.Recommendation:Send the printer to an authorized service center for further repair/diagnosis and proper replacement of the damaged parts.', '2026-01-08', '11:42 AM'),
(1024, 812, '58', 'MARIETTA L. CHUA', 'Vin for your appropriate action', '2026-01-27', '08:19 AM'),
(1025, 811, '59', 'CLEOVIN C. SILONG', 'Upon checking the printer, it was found that its waste inkpad needed to be reset. The EPSON L360 resetter was run successfully, and the printer has now been reset and is currently being used again by the end-user.', '2026-01-27', '12:50 PM'),
(1026, 810, '59', 'CLEOVIN C. SILONG', 'Upon inspection, the printer was found to have no black ink and had previously been repaired for the same issue. Several troubleshooting measures were conducted, including ink flushing and ink pad cleaning; however, no black ink was produced. Eventually, the printer displayed a general error, with unusual motor sounds and no ink pad movement. Ink overflow in the ink tank was also observed. Considering the unit’s age, repeated repairs, and worn-out ink pad, the printer is no longer repairable and is recommended to be declared unserviceable.', '2026-01-27', '12:37 PM');
